{"availability":"available","full":"excellalabs/blog-in-a-box","name":"blog-in-a-box","description":"A quick, all in one stop for someone to get a blog presence up and running.","category":"Other","language":"Shell","stars":10,"forks":4,"created":"2022-03-24T01:36:03Z","updated":"2022-07-09T19:54:45Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://bloginaboxdemo.com","topics":["github-actions","github-pages","hacktoberfest","jekyll","template"],"demo":"https://bloginaboxdemo.com/2022/01/netlify-preview/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T07:22:44.822Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T07:22:44.822Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T07:22:44.822Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T07:22:44.822Z","stars":10,"forks":4}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A quick, all in one stop for someone to get a blog presence up and running.","GitHub Pages, where we presume you are deploying, has some rules for what can be deployed. If deploying from the main branch, you have two options: (root), or the base directory of the repository, and /docs. In our case, we didn't want the other stuff in the root to get confused with the actual blog stuff, so we chose /docs because that's the name available that fits into our batteries-included setup with the least amount of fuss.","There are ways to customize this, particularly by using a gh-pages branch and creating a GitHub Action to push to it, but we figured that might be over-complicated. Feel free to reach out if you want to set that up and we may follow up with some more on this in the future."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/excellalabs/blog-in-a-box/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"461c7202335ff4973f82ee2bb44267c62bef51f3fb804f1a2a008f834a45b29e","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T07:22:45.004Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T07:22:45.004Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A quick, all in one stop for someone to get a blog presence up and runnin